acpid: reap the actions that have ended

acpid sets SIGCHLD to SIG_IGN and never waits for the actions it spawns,
relying on Linux, where a process that ignores SIGCHLD leaves no zombies.
Rach2's kernel keeps the zombie until its parent waits
(rach2/sys/proc/signal.Readme.md), so each key acpid acted on would hold a
slot of the process table for as long as acpid runs. The loop now reaps
every ended child each time poll wakes it, which leaves at most the actions
of the last event unreaped; on Linux the wait finds no child and changes
nothing.

--- a/util-linux/acpid.c
+++ b/util-linux/acpid.c
@@ -329,6 +329,12 @@
 
 	while (safe_poll(pfd, nfd, -1) > 0) {
 		int i;
+
+		/* Reap the actions that have ended: a kernel that does not
+		 * reap the children of a process ignoring SIGCHLD would
+		 * otherwise keep each as a zombie. */
+		while (waitpid(-1, NULL, WNOHANG) > 0)
+			continue;
 		for (i = 0; i < nfd; i++) {
 			const char *event;
 
